    "title": "Catholics across Piedmont Triad celebrate Christmas Eve at Vigil Mass - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Justin Lundy ,\n1 hours ago\n(WGHP) — Many churches in the Piedmont Triad hosted Christmas Eve Vigil Mass, a service where everyone is invited to reflect on the reason for the season.\nEvery voice was raised as members carried candles to the altar on Christmas Eve at Our Lady of Grace Catholic Church in Greensboro.\nSaxapahaw church displaced by flooding forges new bonds with neighboring church Some parishioners say worshiping on Christmas Eve isn’t just a church tradition but a family one.\n“Well, it’s Christmas Eve of course. This is a place where my grandmother used to go,” Matt Campbell said.\nThose who attended mass reflected on how their faith helped them navigate through the trials and tribulations they experienced this year.\n“I recently had surgery. It’s not going to be the most comfortable thing for me. But being here is the most important thing that I can do to show my worship to God,” Ricardo Vargas said.\nAs the countdown to the new year begins, some people say they’re preparing to embark on new spiritual journeys in 2026.\n“The beginning of December marks the beginning of the church year,” Chris Miorin said. “This time we’ve been spending preparing our hearts and our souls for the arrival of Jesus. So as we head into the new year, it’s really a time to go live out those things that we’ve preparing our hearts to do.”\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX8 WGHP.",
